WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.061 --> 00:00:15.703
Shakespeare Smith had sent the boys an invitation to a special ball.

2
00:00:15.723 --> 00:00:22.367
"It says here, Nat, that you should bring your violin so everyone can dance," Tommy said.

3
00:00:22.387 --> 00:00:27.250
"And it indicates that we must behave if we want anything to eat."

4
00:00:28.670 --> 00:00:33.849
"I've never been to a ball," Nat said, "and who is Mrs.

5
00:00:33.989 --> 00:00:35.349
Shakespeare Smith?"

6
00:00:36.830 --> 00:00:37.750
Demi grinned.

7
00:00:37.770 --> 00:00:41.492
"That's a name Daisy uses sometimes.

8
00:00:42.792 --> 00:00:47.294
She pretends she's a grown-up, and Nan is her daughter, Miss Smith."

9
00:00:47.314 --> 00:00:53.657
"The ball's today at three o'clock in the playroom," Jack said, looking at the invitation.

10
00:00:53.677 --> 00:00:55.798
"I have to help Mr.

11
00:00:55.858 --> 00:00:58.779
Bauer then, but I don't want to go to the ball anyway."

12
00:00:58.799 --> 00:01:04.365
"I do—I smelled something delicious cooking," Demi said.

13
00:01:04.385 --> 00:01:12.429
"You know," Tommy said after a moment's thought, "we could leave right after we eat."

14
00:01:12.449 --> 00:01:16.210
"So let's write back and say we'll come," Nat said.

15
00:01:18.071 --> 00:01:23.713
After receiving the boys' note, Daisy was excited, but Nan was concerned.

16
00:01:23.733 --> 00:01:32.117
"Demi and Nat will be good, but Tommy will misbehave," she said, arranging some cupcakes on a plate.

17
00:01:32.137 --> 00:01:35.939
"Then I'll send him right back downstairs!"

18
00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:37.760
Daisy said firmly.

19
00:01:39.021 --> 00:01:39.801
Nan nodded.

20
00:01:39.821 --> 00:01:44.284
"It's almost three o'clock, and we ought to get dressed," she said.

21
00:01:44.304 --> 00:01:48.466
"Come here, Bess, and I'll tie your apron."

22
00:01:49.767 --> 00:01:54.450
Laurie and Amy's four-year-old daughter was visiting and wanted to play the maid.

23
00:01:56.531 --> 00:02:02.711
Daisy put on a pair of glasses, one of Jo's old shawls, and a nightcap decorated with a

24
00:02:02.811 --> 00:02:03.432
red bow.

25
00:02:05.654 --> 00:02:11.038
Nan's outfit included a long skirt, old pink slippers, and a yellow scarf.

26
00:02:12.499 --> 00:02:18.404
Suddenly there was a loud knock at the door, which caused Miss Smith to fly into a chair

27
00:02:18.724 --> 00:02:21.006
and fan herself with a feather duster.

28
00:02:22.527 --> 00:02:26.310
Bess answered the door and said, "Come in, gentlemen!

29
00:02:26.831 --> 00:02:28.052
Everything's ready!"

30
00:02:32.732 --> 00:02:37.897
In honor of the occasion, the boys wore tall black hats and gloves of every color.

31
00:02:39.098 --> 00:02:41.420
None of them owned a matching pair of gloves.

32
00:02:41.440 --> 00:02:47.885
"Good afternoon, ma'am," Demi said in a deep voice.

33
00:02:49.366 --> 00:02:54.571
Everyone shook hands and then sat down, trying to look like serious adults.

34
00:02:59.595 --> 00:03:00.496
stop that!"

35
00:03:00.880 --> 00:03:04.123
Mrs. Smith cried as the boys shook with laughter.

36
00:03:04.143 --> 00:03:09.107
"You can't come again, if you act like that!"

37
00:03:10.308 --> 00:03:14.872
Miss Smith hit Tommy with her fan because he was laughing the hardest.

38
00:03:16.153 --> 00:03:22.338
"I can't help it—you both look so funny!"

39
00:03:23.159 --> 00:03:26.482
"So do you, but I wouldn't be rude enough to tell you!"

40
00:03:29.044 --> 00:03:32.406
Mrs. Smith realized that the ball was getting out of control.

41
00:03:32.426 --> 00:03:35.788
"I think we'd better dance now."

42
00:03:35.808 --> 00:03:38.009
"Let's eat first!"

43
00:03:39.290 --> 00:03:42.912
Tommy winked at Demi to remind him they could soon leave.

44
00:03:42.932 --> 00:03:49.356
"We never eat first, and if you don't dance nicely, you won't get anything to eat."

45
00:03:50.837 --> 00:03:56.740
Mrs. Smith grabbed Tommy by the hand and announced, "Now I will teach you the polka."

46
00:03:58.556 --> 00:04:04.741
Miss Smith danced with Demi, and Nat played his violin while the two couples danced until they were

47
00:04:04.901 --> 00:04:14.769
exhausted. must ask my daughter to play and sing," Mrs.

48
00:04:14.829 --> 00:04:16.931
Smith said, flopping into a chair.

49
00:04:16.951 --> 00:04:23.276
"Give us a song, miss," said Demi, wondering where the piano was.

50
00:04:25.152 --> 00:04:29.454
Miss Smith sailed over to an old desk, which she pretended to play.

51
00:04:31.856 --> 00:04:34.517
After far too many songs, Mrs.

52
00:04:34.597 --> 00:04:37.539
Smith finally said, "It's time for tea."

53
00:04:39.700 --> 00:04:44.002
Unfortunately, things went wrong right from the beginning of teatime.

54
00:04:45.043 --> 00:04:49.825
The best pie fell on the floor, and the boys gobbled up all the bread and butter.

55
00:04:51.506 --> 00:04:56.493
Miss Smith and the maid fought over the best cupcake, which left the maid in tears.

56
00:05:05.881 --> 00:05:08.202
what's happened to my special tarts?"

57
00:05:08.663 --> 00:05:09.844
Mrs. Smith asked.

58
00:05:11.425 --> 00:05:15.047
"I put a raisin on each one and sprinkled them with sugar."

59
00:05:16.669 --> 00:05:20.592
Everyone looked high and low, but the tarts could not be found.

60
00:05:24.720 --> 00:05:26.482
"I know you hid them, Tommy!"

61
00:05:26.762 --> 00:05:28.483
the outraged hostess cried.

62
00:05:28.503 --> 00:05:30.365
"Did not!"

63
00:05:30.645 --> 00:05:31.346
Tommy said.

64
00:05:31.366 --> 00:05:33.568
"Demi stole them."

65
00:05:33.588 --> 00:05:36.570
"What!" Demi cried.

66
00:05:36.590 --> 00:05:39.933
"You probably have them in your pockets!"

67
00:05:39.953 --> 00:05:43.216
"Let's take them away from Tommy!"

68
00:05:43.516 --> 00:05:46.518
said Nat, surprised at how exciting a ball could be.

69
00:05:48.520 --> 00:05:52.723
Tommy fled behind a table and pelted his friends with the stolen tarts.

70
00:05:54.892 --> 00:06:00.457
When Tommy ran out of tarts to throw, Demi and Nat dragged him into the hall and left

71
00:06:00.497 --> 00:06:00.898
him there.

72
00:06:03.340 --> 00:06:05.702
While Demi consoled poor Mrs.

73
00:06:05.802 --> 00:06:09.106
Smith and her maid, Nat collected the tarts.

74
00:06:11.368 --> 00:06:15.412
Then Miss Smith replaced the raisins and put a tart on each plate.

75
00:06:15.432 --> 00:06:18.615
"There—good as new!"

76
00:06:18.975 --> 00:06:19.816
Miss Smith said.

77
00:06:21.036 --> 00:06:25.777
But no one was interested in eating the tarts after they'd been tossed around the room.

78
00:06:25.797 --> 00:06:33.079
"I guess we'd better go," Demi said suddenly as he heard Jo coming up the stairs.

79
00:06:33.099 --> 00:06:38.641
"Perhaps we should," Nat said, hastily stuffing a cupcake into his pocket.

80
00:06:39.941 --> 00:06:45.763
But Jo arrived before the boys could leave, and the girls poured out their tale of woe.

81
00:06:47.603 --> 00:06:50.464
Jo looked sternly at the boys as she scolded them.

82
00:06:51.812 --> 00:06:57.896
"No more balls until you've made up for your bad behavior by doing something nice for the girls."

83
00:06:59.857 --> 00:07:05.020
Nat and Demi bowed their heads, murmuring, "We're sorry."

84
00:07:06.841 --> 00:07:07.622
"I'm not!"

85
00:07:07.902 --> 00:07:11.344
Tommy shouted through the keyhole, where he'd been eavesdropping.

86
00:07:12.825 --> 00:07:14.746
Jo struggled to keep a straight face.

87
00:07:15.966 --> 00:07:23.127
"You may leave, boys, but remember: no talking to or playing with the girls until I give you

88
00:07:23.187 --> 00:07:28.590
permission." The boys ran downstairs as fast as they could.

89
00:07:29.590 --> 00:07:35.073
Tommy pretended not to care and said he could do without "those stupid girls."

90
00:07:39.476 --> 00:07:44.139
Demi and Nat wanted to make up right away, but Daisy and Nan ignored them.

91
00:07:45.479 --> 00:07:52.065
Worst of all, Jo seemed to consider herself one of the offended girls, so she hardly spoke to

92
00:07:52.106 --> 00:07:54.288
the boys and had no time for them.

93
00:07:55.489 --> 00:07:57.771
Jo's coldness bothered even Tommy.

94
00:07:57.791 --> 00:08:02.676
"We're in real trouble now," he admitted.
